NAME
       chmod - change file mode bits

SYNOPSIS
       chmod [-Rvcf] MODE FILE...

DESCRIPTION
       Change the permission bits of each FILE. MODE is an octal number (755,
       0644) or a symbolic list of [ugoa][+-=][rwxXst] clauses separated by
       commas.

OPTIONS
       -R
           change files and directories recursively

       -v
           output a diagnostic for every file processed

       -c
           like -v but report only when a change is made

       -f
           suppress most error messages

EXAMPLES
       chmod 755 script.sh
       chmod u+x,go-w file
       chmod -R a+rX /root/share

SEE ALSO
       ls(1), stat(1)
